  keySpec: Crew ingress and egress
  summary: The main crew access hatch. It is how astronauts board on the pad and
    how recovery teams reach them after splashdown.
  whyItMatters: 'It is a plug design: cabin pressure pushes it harder into its seal
    rather than out of it. With the cabin pressurised and vacuum outside, the hatch
    cannot be opened at all. That is a structural property, not a procedure someone
    has to remember.'
